WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.200
Okay.

00:04.200 --> 00:08.840
So now we're going to check the scenarios and use cases where it makes sense to use CTAs.

00:08.880 --> 00:10.280
So let's start with the first one.

00:10.280 --> 00:16.600
Now we have learned before it makes sense to have a complex logic stored inside a database so that our

00:16.600 --> 00:22.320
end users don't have to keep repeating the same logic over and over, and it's as well maybe complicated

00:22.320 --> 00:23.360
for some users.

00:23.360 --> 00:25.000
So that's why we have used views.

00:25.000 --> 00:27.960
And the result of the view can be used from our users.

00:27.960 --> 00:31.840
So everything can stay easy and friendly to consume for our users.

00:31.840 --> 00:38.600
But now what might happen that the logic of the view could be very complicated and needs a lot of time

00:38.600 --> 00:44.600
to be executed from the database, so it takes really long time until we get the intermediate result

00:44.600 --> 00:45.560
from the database.

00:45.560 --> 00:51.680
So that means if it's going to take 30 minutes, then each user has to wait 30 minutes until the query

00:51.680 --> 00:52.600
is executed.

00:52.600 --> 00:55.600
And none of your users are going to be happy with this situation.

00:55.600 --> 01:00.160
In this scenario, if this happens, you have to try maybe to optimize the query.

01:00.160 --> 01:05.960
But if you cannot do anything about that, you have to switch the view to a CTAs table.

01:05.960 --> 01:12.370
So now what you have to do, you have to take the same logic and then put it in CTAs so that the intermediate

01:12.370 --> 01:14.370
results are stored in a table.

01:14.410 --> 01:18.330
And of course, at the moment of creating the table, it will take 30 minutes.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.450
It will take long time because it is the same query, and the database is going to need the time until

01:23.730 --> 01:25.570
creating the intermediate results.

01:25.570 --> 01:31.330
But the big advantage is that once everything is prepared, maybe at the night and the morning, once

01:31.330 --> 01:37.130
your users are like online and start querying the data, they have everything prepared.

01:37.130 --> 01:42.690
So the user is going to go and start selecting and analyzing the intermediate result, but this time

01:42.690 --> 01:46.050
using the table that you have created from the CTAs.

01:46.130 --> 01:50.130
And the response time is going to be for all users again, normal and fast.

01:50.130 --> 01:55.330
So if you have a scenario where your views are very slow, you have to go and prepare the data at night

01:55.330 --> 02:00.610
using the Ctace and prepare the tables to be analyzed from the end users.

02:00.610 --> 02:03.330
So this is the most common use case for the Ctace.

02:03.490 --> 02:10.010
And this scenario happens a lot in projects where you decide to go instead of use to go with the ctace

02:10.050 --> 02:13.210
in order to have data, and you gain performance.

02:13.250 --> 02:13.570
Okay.

02:13.610 --> 02:15.170
So finally back to SQL.

02:15.330 --> 02:17.650
Let's go and create a table using CTAs.

02:17.690 --> 02:22.650
Now we're going to go and create a table that shows the total number of orders for each month.

02:22.690 --> 02:23.610
Let's go and do it.

02:23.610 --> 02:24.610
So first what do we need.

02:24.650 --> 02:25.690
We need a query.

02:25.690 --> 02:29.650
So let's write it select I'm going to go with the date name.

02:29.650 --> 02:34.610
In order to get the name of the month from our order date.

02:34.610 --> 02:37.570
And we're going to call it order month.

02:37.930 --> 02:47.010
And then we're going to go and aggregate the data by counting the order ID for total orders from our

02:47.010 --> 02:49.570
table sales orders.

02:49.810 --> 02:52.610
And don't forget to group by our month.

02:52.610 --> 02:54.410
So something like this.

02:55.330 --> 02:56.850
Let's go and execute it.

02:56.850 --> 02:58.330
So the result is very simple.

02:58.330 --> 03:00.890
We have the order month and the total orders.

03:00.890 --> 03:03.290
So we have two columns and three rows.

03:03.290 --> 03:04.290
So we have our query.

03:04.290 --> 03:06.290
And of course we didn't create anything yet.

03:06.330 --> 03:13.050
Now in SQL server in order to create a table from the query, what we're going to do exactly before

03:13.050 --> 03:15.130
the from, we're going to write into.

03:15.170 --> 03:17.980
And now we have to specify the schema and the table name.

03:17.980 --> 03:25.140
I'm gonna stay with the schema sales, and I'm going to call it monthly orders like this.

03:25.140 --> 03:27.140
So that means we have our query.

03:27.140 --> 03:30.540
And the DDL is exactly between the from and select.

03:30.540 --> 03:33.980
So now if I go and execute this what's going to happen.

03:33.980 --> 03:36.220
We will not see here the result of the query.

03:36.260 --> 03:38.660
We're going to get here like three rows affected.

03:38.660 --> 03:40.540
Because this is DDL statement.

03:40.540 --> 03:42.180
It is not anymore query.

03:42.180 --> 03:45.980
And the database is telling us I have created now a table with three rows.

03:46.020 --> 03:48.060
Now if you check our tables we don't see it yet.

03:48.060 --> 03:50.740
Let's go and refresh and check again the tables.

03:50.780 --> 03:52.580
Now we can see our table here.

03:52.780 --> 03:54.500
Sales monthly orders.

03:54.540 --> 03:57.140
Now of course we have to go and check whether everything is fine.

03:57.460 --> 04:04.420
So let's go and select the rows from our new table sales monthly orders.

04:05.820 --> 04:09.180
So let's go select it first and execute.

04:09.180 --> 04:12.380
And now we can see again the result of our query.

04:12.380 --> 04:13.940
But we are not writing the query.

04:13.940 --> 04:15.820
We are just selecting it from the table.

04:15.820 --> 04:18.580
So our data is stored in our table.

04:18.580 --> 04:21.260
And we can go and check the structure of this table.

04:21.260 --> 04:25.990
So if we go to the columns, you can see we have here the order month and the total orders.

04:25.990 --> 04:28.390
And those information comes from our query.

04:28.390 --> 04:33.990
So psql is saying here the order month is varchar which is correct because here we have the names of

04:33.990 --> 04:34.470
the month.

04:34.470 --> 04:39.430
So psql is able to define the data type of the table from our query.

04:39.430 --> 04:41.310
And the second column the total orders.

04:41.310 --> 04:42.390
It is an integer.

04:42.390 --> 04:43.950
And that's because we have here numbers.

04:43.950 --> 04:50.830
So as you can see SQL is defining the structure of the table based on the result of our query over here.

04:50.830 --> 04:54.150
And of course the data inside the table comes as well from the query.

04:54.150 --> 04:58.430
And the result of this table can stay like this as long as you don't change anything.

04:58.430 --> 05:03.590
So if you go and close this and open it after one year, it's going to show exact same results.

05:03.590 --> 05:07.310
So it's going to live in the database as long as you don't drop this table.

05:07.350 --> 05:13.030
But if things change in the table orders, this table will not be updated automatically like we have

05:13.030 --> 05:14.150
learned in the views.

05:14.150 --> 05:17.230
So now if you want to say you know what, I would like to go and drop this table.

05:17.230 --> 05:18.630
Well it is very simple.

05:18.750 --> 05:23.150
Just go and say drop table and the table name over here.

05:23.150 --> 05:25.630
So make sure you select it and execute it.

05:25.630 --> 05:28.120
And now if you go over here and refresh.

05:28.160 --> 05:29.440
So let's check the tables.

05:29.440 --> 05:31.840
You can see here the table is dropped.

05:35.760 --> 05:41.920
And now if you say you know what, let's go and refresh the table that come from the CTAs every day

05:41.920 --> 05:45.080
so that we always get refresh data inside this table.

05:45.400 --> 05:48.160
So now let's go and execute again our CTAs.

05:48.280 --> 05:52.520
And with that, if we go and refresh we're gonna find again our table inside it.

05:52.520 --> 05:57.600
Now if you go and execute it one more time in order to refresh the data of the table, what are you

05:57.600 --> 05:57.920
gonna get?

05:57.920 --> 05:58.800
You're going to get an error.

05:58.840 --> 06:02.840
The database is going to tell you we have already this table so we cannot recreate it.

06:02.840 --> 06:06.760
So now the question is how we can update then the content of this table.

06:06.760 --> 06:10.120
Well we have to go and drop it first and then recreate it.

06:10.120 --> 06:16.280
And if you want to put everything in one statement we have to go and use the Tsql is Transact-sql.

06:16.320 --> 06:20.760
It's like extension where you can do some programming inside SQL.

06:20.760 --> 06:25.160
So in order to do that, what we're going to do, we're going to go at the start over here and we're

06:25.160 --> 06:26.600
going to make an if logic.

06:26.600 --> 06:29.040
So we're going to go and search for the objects.

06:29.040 --> 06:35.520
So we're going to say if the object ID and now we have to go and specify the name of this object together

06:35.520 --> 06:36.360
with the schema.

06:36.400 --> 06:40.640
Make sure to select everything sales monthly order and put it inside here.

06:41.040 --> 06:44.760
And then we have to define the type of this object.

06:44.760 --> 06:46.160
And here we're going to go with you.

06:46.200 --> 06:48.520
It is user defined table.

06:48.520 --> 06:54.560
So we are saying if the object sales monthly orders is not null.

06:54.560 --> 06:56.360
So that means it exists.

06:56.480 --> 06:59.040
So what you want to do we have to go and drop it.

06:59.040 --> 07:00.960
I'm going to take the statement from here.

07:00.960 --> 07:04.320
And then we're going to put it after the if over here.

07:04.320 --> 07:08.240
So we are saying if this table exists then drop the table.

07:08.440 --> 07:13.320
Otherwise don't do anything because we don't have any new table and the query can work.

07:13.320 --> 07:18.360
And at the end of the tsql we have to go in order to say that T-sql is done.

07:18.360 --> 07:20.720
And then our usual query after that.

07:20.720 --> 07:23.120
So let's go and execute the whole thing.

07:23.640 --> 07:25.520
And as you can see it is working.

07:25.520 --> 07:26.280
So what happens.

07:26.280 --> 07:31.400
The database did find this table and drop it and then executed our query.

07:31.400 --> 07:35.880
So if you keep executing this you are just refreshing the content of this table.

07:35.880 --> 07:39.000
So this is how we work with the CTAs in SQL.
